# =============================================================================
# SECURITY NOTICE - DO NOT COMMIT, SHARE, OR BACK UP UNENCRYPTED
# =============================================================================
# The runtime `.env` derived from this template will hold regulated personal
# data: at minimum the operator's real DNI / NIE and NIE support number
# (Cl@ve Móvil identity), optional AEAT proxy credentials, and the master-key
# passphrase. These are AEAT-regulated identifiers under Spanish tax law.
#
# - `.env` is git-ignored. Never override that ignore. Never `git add -f .env`.
# - Do not copy `.env` into cloud-synced folders (Dropbox, OneDrive, iCloud).
# - Do not share `.env` over chat, email, ticket attachments, or screen-share.
# - If you suspect leakage, rotate every secret in the file immediately and
#   notify the responsible party (NIE rotation requires AEAT contact; the
#   master passphrase can be rotated locally via the wallet CLI).
# =============================================================================

# -- How this file is used -----------------------------------------------------
# Every name below is a process environment variable. A blank value means unset;
# a commented line is an optional tooling knob.
#
# `just init` provisions Python/tooling, copies this template to env/.env
# when absent, and publishes registry authority. Existing env/.env files
# are preserved. It also provisions and verifies Playwright browser resources;
# installing missing Linux system resources requires root or passwordless sudo.
# It does not supply credentials.
# Product Settings read the process environment, not this file. For CLI/dev
# commands, load it explicitly with `uv run --no-sync --env-file env/.env ...`.
# Repository pytest bridges env/.env into unset process variables; values
# supplied by the runner take precedence. Test output paths are prepared
# before that bridge, so configure those in the runner's process environment.
# Setup-only secrets do not cover live tests executed later in the task.
#
# Cl@ve Móvil with an NIE needs these private values:
# - CADRUMO_CLAVE_MOVIL_DNI_NIE: taxpayer NIE.
# - CADRUMO_CLAVE_MOVIL_NIE_SOPORTE: NIE support number.
# - CADRUMO_SECRET_PASSPHRASE: headless encrypted secret-store passphrase.
# Use a private passphrase for live data, never the published test password.
# Login still requires approval in the Cl@ve app on the operator's phone.
# The default app-request login respects CADRUMO_BROWSER_HEADLESS. Setting
# CADRUMO_CLAVE_PREFER_NON_QR=false selects QR scanning, which always opens a
# visible browser because the code must be seen.
# Optional secrets depend on the exercised integration:
# CADRUMO_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD_SECRET plus the private certificate bundle; CADRUMO_CLAVE_PERMANENTE_PASSWORD for that provider;
# or CADRUMO_PROXY_PASSWORD_SECRET for an authenticated browser proxy.
# Google refresh tokens are registered in Cadrumo's encrypted store.
# Documentation delivery credentials below are needed only for publication.

# -- Publisher Google Desktop OAuth --------------------------------------------
# Full Google client download with its installed envelope, on one quoted line.
# Supply privately for development/builds; CI uses the matching repository secret.
# Release artifacts embed this identity. Keep the actual JSON out of source control.
# Run `uv run --no-sync python -m dev.env setup` after changing it to refresh
# the ignored development resource used by isolated profile workers.
CADRUMO_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_JSON=

# -- Storage roots -------------------------------------------------------------
# All application, test and development storage follows CADRUMO_STORAGE_ROOT.
# Its default is var/storage beneath the repository. Relative roots anchor to
# the repository; relative per-storage overrides anchor beneath the storage root.
# Absolute overrides relocate a category independently. Empty values are unset.
#
# Shared development storage root; every location below derives from it.
CADRUMO_STORAGE_ROOT=var/storage
# Local backend root; wins over CADRUMO_STORAGE_ROOT and is refused when relative in a package.
CADRUMO_LOCAL_STORAGE_ROOT=
# Backend for the outbound storage adapter. One of: local_filesystem
# (default), google_drive, in_memory. google_drive additionally requires a
# Google sign-in for the profile through `aeat config google login`.
CADRUMO_STORAGE_PROVIDER_KIND=local_filesystem
# Temporary application files.
CADRUMO_TEMP_DIR=
# Local connection sockets; POSIX sockets need a short path, so an absolute override may be required.
CADRUMO_RUNTIME_SOCKET_DIR=
# Alternate spelling of CADRUMO_RUNTIME_SOCKET_DIR; the runtime spelling takes precedence.
CADRUMO_CONNECTION_SOCKET_DIR=
# Managed Playwright browser binaries.
CADRUMO_PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_DIR=
# Chromium working profiles; empty follows the storage root, a relative value resolves beneath it.
# Saved authentication state stays in encrypted profile storage.
CADRUMO_CHROMIUM_DATA_ROOT=
# Optional SQLAlchemy URL for controlled storage diagnostics. Leave this empty
# for normal use so the active profile selects its own bucket database.
CADRUMO_DATABASE_URL=

# -- Profile data locations ----------------------------------------------------
# Empty values derive beneath the storage root; give an absolute path to relocate one.
# Cached authentication tokens.
CADRUMO_TOKEN_DIR=
# Encrypted secret-store master-key file and the ciphertext records it persists.
CADRUMO_SECRET_STORE_DIR=
# Encrypted blob store (content-addressed, classification-aware). CORPUS-class
# blobs are stored as plaintext; every other class is stored as ciphertext.
CADRUMO_BLOB_STORE_DIR=
# Live AEAT state and remote-state evidence.
CADRUMO_LIVE_STATE_DIR=
# Transaction catalogue JSON file.
CADRUMO_FINANCIAL_TXS_DIR=
# Invoice catalogue JSON file.
CADRUMO_INVOICES_DIR=
# Attachment byte and manifest store.
CADRUMO_ATTACHMENTS_DIR=
# Per-category usage-ratio overrides file.
CADRUMO_USAGE_RATIOS_PATH=
# SubmittedFiling JSON audit records.
CADRUMO_SUBMISSIONS_DIR=
# Composite-workflow run records (WorkflowResult), one JSON file per run_id.
CADRUMO_WORKFLOW_RUNS_DIR=
# Filing drafts, written as JSON files.
CADRUMO_DRAFTS_DIR=
# Parsed justificante PDFs and their metadata.
CADRUMO_JUSTIFICANTES_DIR=
# Filed-declaration observations captured from AEAT.
CADRUMO_FILED_DECLARATIONS_DIR=
# Modelo 303 compensation-history capture reports.
CADRUMO_IVA_COMPENSATION_HISTORY_DIR=
# IVA remote-state read-evidence reports.
CADRUMO_IVA_READ_EVIDENCE_DIR=
# Persisted FilingHistory JSON file (`history.json`).
CADRUMO_FILING_HISTORY_DIR=
# Append-only local LLM run-timing record logs.
CADRUMO_LLM_RUN_RECORD_DIR=
# LLM response cache.
CADRUMO_LLM_CACHE_DIR=
# LLM usage records.
CADRUMO_LLM_USAGE_DIR=
# Run traces and JSONL event logs, one subdirectory per run_id (trace.json + events.jsonl).
CADRUMO_RUNS_DIR=
# Bundled-corpus search index; empty derives <storage-root>/cache/corpus-search.
CADRUMO_CORPUS_SEARCH_CACHE_DIR=
# Diagnostic-log root; empty uses the project-relative default of the logging helper.
CADRUMO_LOG_DIR=

# -- Presentation and output ---------------------------------------------------
# Default stderr verbosity for the CLI root callback. Leave blank to use the
# contract default; valid values: quiet|default|verbose|debug.
CADRUMO_LOG_LEVEL=
# Force ANSI colour output even when stdout is not a TTY.
CADRUMO_FORCE_COLOR=false
# Disable ANSI colour output regardless of TTY state (no-color.org convention).
NO_COLOR=false
# Reveal raw profile/bucket UUIDs in CLI success output instead of the
# paste-safe <profile-id> / <bucket-id> placeholders. Default off keeps the
# output-redaction policy; a multi-client gestor sets =1 to disambiguate
# which bucket a command addressed. NIF/CIF/NIE, tokens, URLs, and
# secure-object keys stay redacted regardless.
CADRUMO_CLI_REVEAL_IDENTIFIERS=false
# Target output language for every user-facing string. Accepted values
# are ISO 639-1 codes from the quad-lingual contract:
#   es  Spanish     - default, AEAT canonical, legally authoritative
#   en  English     - code/docs working language
#   ca  Catalan     - co-official across CAT / IB / VAL; tax acronyms
#                     (IVA, IRPF) match Spanish per Generalitat usage
#   hu  Hungarian   - operator first language
CADRUMO_OUTPUT_LANGUAGE=es

# -- Logging -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Log level for the stderr handler installed by aeat.core.logging.
CADRUMO_LOG_STDERR_LEVEL=ERROR
# Log level for the file handler installed by aeat.core.logging.
CADRUMO_LOG_FILE_LEVEL=DEBUG
# Size cap (bytes) for cadrumo.log before the rotating handler rolls over.
CADRUMO_LOG_FILE_MAX_BYTES=10485760
# Number of rotated cadrumo.log backups the rotating handler retains.
CADRUMO_LOG_FILE_BACKUP_COUNT=5
# Root logger level installed by aeat.core.logging.
CADRUMO_LOG_ROOT_LEVEL=DEBUG

# -- Secrets and security ------------------------------------------------------
# Passphrase that derives the encrypted-secret-store master key. Leave
# blank to keep the master-key loader fail-closed; set it on CI / headless
# hosts that use the encrypted-file backend.
CADRUMO_SECRET_PASSPHRASE=
# Shared development/test-only database password used by secure-storage
# test helpers. This is a published non-production constant; do not use
# it for operator profiles or live taxpayer data.
CADRUMO_DEV_TEST_DATABASE_PASSWORD=aeat-dev-test-database-password
# Development only: allow same-account CLI/TUI/MCP connections across OS sessions.
# Load this into the manually started runtime; clients cannot enable the override.
# Exactly 1 disables desktop/session admission; unset or 0 keeps strict checking.
# Native account identity, profile credentials, grants and connection binding remain.
# This does not start, install or register a runtime.
CADRUMO_DEV_RUNTIME_SESSION_OVERRIDE=1
# Whether profile-custody KDF calibration MEASURES the parameter grid on this
# host. true (the default, and the only production posture) samples real
# supervised derivations to pick the strongest grid point that still lands
# inside the operator latency band. false skips the measurement loop and adopts
# the fixed fallback point the calibrator already uses when no point can be
# confirmed in time.
#
# Measuring can only strengthen a wrap: calibration never selects a point
# weaker than the fallback, so false leaves every new profile at the fallback's
# strength. The derivation is the same real Argon2id through the same
# supervised worker either way.
CADRUMO_PROFILE_KDF_MEASURE_CALIBRATION=true

# -- AEAT portal ---------------------------------------------------------------
# No AEAT live-submit variables exist. The product is produce -> verify -> export,
# and the operator uploads the exported file through the AEAT portal.
# AEAT Sede URL that `aeat config repair connectivity` navigates to when probing
# for a mantenimiento banner, a WAF challenge, or a rate-limit answer.
SITE_HEALTH_PROBE_URL=https://sede.agenciatributaria.gob.es/
# Fallback Retry-After (seconds) used by the rate-limit parser when
# a 429/503 response omits the Retry-After header.
SITE_HEALTH_RATE_LIMIT_RETRY_AFTER_DEFAULT=300
# AEAT auth-method selector page template - {target} is replaced with
# the URL-encoded post-auth target (defaults to Mis expedientes).
# Rarely overridden; exposed for pre-prod portal swaps.
AEAT_CLAVE_SEDE_ACCESS_URL_TEMPLATE=https://sede.agenciatributaria.gob.es/static_files/common/html/selector_acceso/SelectorAccesos.html?rep=S&ref={target}&aut=CP
# AEAT auth-method selector page template for Cl@ve Permanente - {target} is
# replaced with the URL-encoded post-auth target. Rarely overridden; exposed
# for pre-prod portal swaps.
AEAT_CLAVE_PERMANENTE_SEDE_ACCESS_URL_TEMPLATE=https://sede.agenciatributaria.gob.es/static_files/common/html/selector_acceso/SelectorAccesos.html?rep=S&ref={target}&aut=CP
# AEAT Sede path for Mis expedientes - the default target used by
# `aeat auth login --provider clave_movil` and the expedientes reader.
AEAT_SEDE_EXPEDIENTES_PATH=/wlpl/TEWV-CORE/ResumenVlt

# -- Browser automation (Playwright) -------------------------------------------
# Run the browser in headless mode; QR login always opens a visible browser.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_HEADLESS=true
# Default browser locale passed to Playwright context (BCP-47 tag).
CADRUMO_BROWSER_LOCALE=es-ES
# Default IANA timezone string passed to Playwright context.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_TIMEZONE=Europe/Madrid
# Default Playwright viewport width (pixels) for AEAT sede sessions.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_VIEWPORT_WIDTH=1366
# Default Playwright viewport height (pixels) for AEAT sede sessions.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_VIEWPORT_HEIGHT=900
# Default Playwright navigation timeout (ms) for AEAT sede pages.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_NAVIGATION_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# Timeout for individual form interactions (fill / click / wait) in ms.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_FORM_INTERACTION_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# Timeout (ms) for the AEAT declarations 'Ver' button click + navigation.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_VER_CLICK_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# Settle delay (ms) after the AEAT 'Buscar' button before reading results.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_BUSCAR_SETTLE_MS=3000
# Selector visibility probe timeout (ms) for GROI / NIF-IVA check stages.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_SELECTOR_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=2500
# Best-effort timeout (ms) for Playwright browser context/session cleanup.
CADRUMO_BROWSER_CLOSE_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
# Outer timeout (ms) for each live IVA filed-history or wallet/cartera read surface.
CADRUMO_LIVE_IVA_SURFACE_TIMEOUT_MS=180000
# Timeout (ms) for one Modelo 303 declaration observation inside filed-history capture.
CADRUMO_LIVE_IVA_DECLARATION_CAPTURE_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# Timeout (ms) for one filed-declaration register query for a single modelo/year.
CADRUMO_LIVE_FILED_REGISTER_WALK_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# Drain delay (ms) for cancellation-only Playwright errors after bounded live IVA reads.
CADRUMO_LIVE_IVA_CANCELLATION_DRAIN_MS=250
# Proxy URL (for example http://proxy.example.com:8080); empty means a direct connection.
CADRUMO_PROXY_URL=
# Username for proxy authentication.
CADRUMO_PROXY_USERNAME=
# Password for proxy authentication; env var only, never logged.
CADRUMO_PROXY_PASSWORD_SECRET=
# Comma-separated list of domains that bypass the proxy.
CADRUMO_PROXY_BYPASS=

# -- Authentication: provider selection and locks ------------------------------
# Picks the default provider used by `aeat auth login` / `status` when
# --provider is omitted. Valid values: certificate, clave_permanente,
# clave_movil, clave_pin. Leave blank to auto-pick the first configured
# provider (certificate is preferred when both are configured).
CADRUMO_AUTH_PROVIDER=
# Headroom (seconds) added to CADRUMO_CLAVE_MOVIL_TIMEOUT_MS for the lock TTL.
CADRUMO_AUTH_CLAVE_MOVIL_LOCK_BUFFER_S=90
# Acquisition lock TTL (seconds) for certificate-backed AEAT auth flows.
CADRUMO_AUTH_CERTIFICATE_LOCK_TTL_S=180
# Default exclusive file-lock acquisition timeout (seconds).
CADRUMO_FILE_LOCK_TIMEOUT_S=30.0
# Sleep interval (seconds) between non-blocking file-lock acquire attempts.
CADRUMO_FILE_LOCK_RETRY_BACKOFF_S=0.05
# Polling interval (seconds) for bucket lockfile acquisition retries.
CADRUMO_BUCKET_LOCK_POLL_INTERVAL_S=0.1
# Fallback idle-lock window (minutes) when a bucket manifest omits it.
CADRUMO_BUCKET_DEFAULT_IDLE_LOCK_MINUTES=15
# Fallback absolute session cap (minutes) when a bucket manifest omits it.
# Fixed at login and never refreshed; validated to the 60-720 range.
CADRUMO_BUCKET_DEFAULT_SESSION_ABSOLUTE_MINUTES=240

# -- Authentication: certificate -----------------------------------------------
# PKCS#12 (.p12/.pfx) bundle supplied by the operator. Issued by FNMT-RCM
# as a "certificado de persona fisica".
CADRUMO_CERTIFICATE_PATH=
# PKCS#12 passphrase; env var only, never logged or persisted.
CADRUMO_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD_SECRET=
# Optional human-readable label for the certificate.
CADRUMO_CERTIFICATE_FRIENDLY_NAME=
# Pre-expiry gate thresholds. Certificates with <= CADRUMO_CERT_WARN_DAYS
# remaining surface as WARN; <= CADRUMO_CERT_CRITICAL_DAYS as CRITICAL and
# must be renewed before authenticated AEAT work continues.
CADRUMO_CERT_WARN_DAYS=60
CADRUMO_CERT_CRITICAL_DAYS=14

# -- Authentication: Cl@ve Móvil -----------------------------------------------
# Taxpayer DNI or NIE for `aeat auth login --provider clave_movil`.
# Stamped onto the persisted session and typed into the default app-request
# form. Treat it as private runner configuration; the Cl@ve app
# on your phone supplies the approval factor.
CADRUMO_CLAVE_MOVIL_DNI_NIE=
# DNI validity / expiry date (YYYY-MM-DD) - needed by the default
# app-request Cl@ve Móvil route when the identity is a DNI.
CADRUMO_CLAVE_MOVIL_DNI_FECHA=
# NIE support number (número de soporte) - needed by the default
# app-request Cl@ve Móvil route when the identity is a NIE.
CADRUMO_CLAVE_MOVIL_NIE_SOPORTE=
# Cl@ve Móvil route when the profile has not chosen one. true (the default)
# identifies with DNI/NIE + contraste and sends an approval request to the
# Cl@ve app on your phone; false scans a QR code in a visible browser.
CADRUMO_CLAVE_PREFER_NON_QR=true
# Maximum wait (milliseconds) for operator to approve the push
# notification on the phone. The Settings model caps this at 120000 (fail
# fast enough for an operator to retry), so the template uses that ceiling.
CADRUMO_CLAVE_MOVIL_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# -- Authentication: Cl@ve Permanente ------------------------------------------
# Taxpayer DNI or NIE for `aeat auth login --provider clave_permanente`.
# Used as the Cl@ve IdP login username.
CADRUMO_CLAVE_PERMANENTE_DNI_NIE=
# Cl@ve Permanente password. Same treatment as the certificate
# passphrase: env var only, never a committed value, never logged.
CADRUMO_CLAVE_PERMANENTE_PASSWORD=
# Maximum wait (milliseconds) for the Cl@ve Permanente login form
# round-trip. Routine login is headless-automatable (DNI/NIE +
# password, no SMS), so this window is shorter than Cl@ve Móvil's.
CADRUMO_CLAVE_PERMANENTE_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# -- Local models -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Off-host model work goes to the agent service, on the lane the signed-in
# person selected there; no provider key is read from this file.
# Local Ollama /api/chat endpoint (override for non-localhost deployments).
CADRUMO_LLM_OLLAMA_CHAT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat
# Local Ollama vision model used to read scanned/image evidence on-host
# (gestor-allowed default posture); must be a multimodal model pulled locally.
CADRUMO_LLM_OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=qwen3-vl:2b
# Local Ollama TEXT model used to classify a text-layer document on-host;
# reads only extracted text and selects from the registry allow-list.
CADRUMO_LLM_OLLAMA_TEXT_MODEL=qwen3:1.7b
# Local Ollama model used to name what each column of a delimited table holds
# from its header strings alone; sized down independently of the text role.
CADRUMO_LLM_OLLAMA_MAPPING_MODEL=qwen3:1.7b
# Minimum total system memory the local model runtime needs before a vision
# read is worth attempting; below it the runtime thrashes or is killed
# mid-read rather than refusing cleanly.
CADRUMO_LLM_MODEL_RUNTIME_MEMORY_FLOOR_BYTES=8589934592
# Headroom (bytes) kept free above a model's declared memory requirement
# before a local load is admitted, covering KV-cache growth and scratch
# buffers a bare weight-size check would miss.
CADRUMO_LLM_CONTENTION_SAFETY_MARGIN_BYTES=1073741824
# Admit a local model load even when free headroom could not be measured.
# Default false (fails closed); set true only on a machine known to have
# capacity this build cannot read.
CADRUMO_LLM_CONTENTION_CHECK_OVERRIDE=false
# How many on-host inference requests this process may run at once. Default
# one; a request arriving while the arena is full is refused, not queued.
CADRUMO_LLM_LOCAL_INFERENCE_CONCURRENCY=1
# Ollama context window (num_ctx) for local requests; 8192 fits the registry
# allow-list prompt plus the encoded invoice image and output with headroom.
CADRUMO_LLM_OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=8192
# Per-request timeout (seconds) for the on-host local vision read; larger than
# the general LLM timeout because a local vision model can take minutes.
CADRUMO_LLM_VISION_READ_TIMEOUT_S=300
# Default maximum output tokens when an LLM request omits max_tokens.
CADRUMO_LLM_DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS=1024
# Default sampling temperature when an LLM request omits temperature.
CADRUMO_LLM_DEFAULT_TEMPERATURE=0.0
# Default timeout (seconds) for LLM provider calls.
CADRUMO_LLM_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_S=60
# Local LLM run-record retention: records older than this window, or
# beyond this count, are pruned by LLMRunRecorder.prune().
CADRUMO_LLM_RUN_RECORD_RETENTION_DAYS=30
CADRUMO_LLM_RUN_RECORD_MAX_RECORDS=5000
# LLM response-cache retention: entries older than this window, or beyond this
# count, are pruned by LLMCache.prune().
CADRUMO_LLM_CACHE_RETENTION_DAYS=30
CADRUMO_LLM_CACHE_MAX_RECORDS=5000
# LLM usage-record retention: records older than this window, or beyond this
# count, are pruned by UsageRecorder.prune().
CADRUMO_LLM_USAGE_RETENTION_DAYS=30
CADRUMO_LLM_USAGE_MAX_RECORDS=5000

# -- Evidence reading (LLM) ----------------------------------------------------
# Whether this deployment permits reading taxpayer evidence at an off-host
# model at all. Default off: every evidence read stays on the host. When
# true, an explicit per-invocation operator acknowledgement is still
# required for each read, and gestor deployments stay barred.
CADRUMO_EVIDENCE_CLOUD_UPLOAD_PERMITTED=false
# Gestor/professional deployment flag for evidence reading. When true, an
# off-host evidence read is categorically refused regardless of
# CADRUMO_EVIDENCE_CLOUD_UPLOAD_PERMITTED or any per-invocation acknowledgement.
CADRUMO_EVIDENCE_GESTOR_MODE=false

# -- Integrations: Google, FX, financial ingest, corpora -----------------------
# Folder name created under the Google Drive root for the AEAT vault.
CADRUMO_GOOGLE_DRIVE_VAULT_FOLDER_NAME=cadrumo-vault
# Timeout (seconds) for one ECB Data Portal euro reference-rate lookup. A
# ledger import resolves one lookup per distinct currency/date, so this budget
# bounds a single observation query rather than the whole import.
CADRUMO_FX_RATE_LOOKUP_TIMEOUT_S=15
# Fallback ISO 4217 currency used when a financial source does not carry a
# per-row currency column.
FINANCIAL_BASE_CURRENCY=EUR
# Preferred encoding attempted first when decoding CSV bank exports.
FINANCIAL_DEFAULT_CSV_ENCODING=utf-8
# Override the bundled AEAT Manual practico corpus root. Leave unset to
# read the corpus shipped inside the installed package via the resource
# locator. Set to an absolute path when pointing at an external mirror.
# The 'aeat manual fetch' CLI writes PDFs and manifests under this path.
AEAT_MANUALS_ROOT=
# Override the bundled normatives root (Ley 35/2006, Ley 37/1992, LGT,
# RD 439/2007, etc.). Leave unset to read the corpus shipped inside the
# installed package via the resource locator. Set to an absolute path to override.
AEAT_NORMATIVES_ROOT=

# -- Filing and justificantes ---------------------------------------------------
# Parser backend for aeat.justificante. pdfplumber is the fidelity-first
# default; the setting enum value is lowercase.
CADRUMO_JUSTIFICANTE_PARSER_BACKEND=pdfplumber
# Opt-in diagnostic capture directory for the IVA compensation wallet
# (cartera) read. Unset (the default) disables capture; the wallet-read
# path is byte-for-byte unchanged. When set, the wallet read dumps the
# full captured page tree (main document, popups, child frames,
# per-page screenshots) here so AEAT DOM drift on the cartera surface
# can be diagnosed offline. Production must keep this empty.
CADRUMO_WALLET_DIAGNOSTIC_DUMP_DIR=
# Retention window in days for wallet diagnostic dump files (applies only when
# the dump directory above is configured).
CADRUMO_WALLET_DIAGNOSTIC_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# -- Observability -------------------------------------------------------------
# Retention window in days for per-run trace directories; older run
# directories are pruned by prune_run_traces().
CADRUMO_RUNS_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# Total on-disk size cap (bytes) for run traces after age-based pruning.
CADRUMO_RUNS_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES=268435456

# -- Registry authority --------------------------------------------------------
# Directory holding the published registry authority descriptor
# `authority.current.json` and the content-addressed SQLite generation it
# selects. Leave blank for the installed posture: the authority ships inside
# the distribution and resolves through the bundled-data boundary. A
# development checkout that publishes its own authority tree outside the
# packaged location points this at that tree; the descriptor must exist under
# the named directory.
CADRUMO_AUTHORITY_ROOT=

# -- Installed package ---------------------------------------------------------
# Extra existing absolute directories (separated by the platform path separator)
# where an installed package may find external tools such as a provider command
# line. Read by the package launcher, not by Settings.
# CADRUMO_EXTERNAL_BIN_DIRS=

# -- Live tests ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Opt-in flag for `@pytest.mark.aeat_live` tests that hit real external
# services. Must be set to exactly `1` to enable - this is a deliberate
# safety kill-switch, so any other value (including `true`/`false`)
# leaves live tests and live AEAT reads disabled. Default `pytest`
# invocation excludes live tests. Set this to 1 before selecting them with
# `just test-registry-live` or a focused `uv run --no-sync pytest -n0 -m aeat_live`.
# The recipe selects tests; it does not set this flag or provision credentials.
CADRUMO_LIVE_TESTS_ENABLED=0
# Opt-in flag for the Google (OAuth / Drive) live tests. Same exact-`1`
# safety kill-switch as CADRUMO_LIVE_TESTS_ENABLED; requires that flag too.
CADRUMO_LIVE_TESTS_GOOGLE=0
# Additional opt-in read directly by the full Cl@ve Móvil login test.
# Set to exactly 1 only when ready to approve a fresh login on your phone.
CADRUMO_CLAVE_MOVIL_FULL_LIVE_AUTH=0
# External ingestion measurement corpus: the read-only directory holding
# GROUND_TRUTH.json. No default; selected by `just test-ingest-corpus`.
# CADRUMO_INGEST_CORPUS_ROOT=

# -- Test execution and reports ------------------------------------------------
# Development/test controls, not product Settings. Inject path controls before
# starting pytest: env/.env is bridged after its run directories are allocated.
# Optional integer worker count; use 2 for a small cloud runner. If unset,
# `-n auto` uses the project's default. Serial/live tests use -n0 explicitly.
# CADRUMO_PYTEST_WORKERS=2
# Short absolute scratch base, e.g. /tmp/cadrumo or C:/tmp/cadrumo. This moves
# run scratch, not run logs. Unset uses <storage-root>/tmp.
CADRUMO_SCRATCH_BASE=
# Optional JUnit report directory. Unset/blank produces no JUnit report.
VAULTSPEC_CI_REPORTS=
CADRUMO_CI_REPORTS_DIR=
# Optional filename stem, without .xml; use a different stem for each test lane.
# Unset derives a name from the pytest invocation. Explicit --junitxml wins.
VAULTSPEC_CI_REPORT_NAME=
# Pytest logs default beneath <storage-root>/development/.logs/test-runs.
# CADRUMO_TEST_LOG_ROOT independently relocates the log base.
CADRUMO_TEST_LOG_ROOT=
# Run context variables such as CADRUMO_TEST_RUN_ROOT and CADRUMO_TEST_RUN_SCRATCH
# are assigned by the runner; TEMP/TMP/TMPDIR follow its controlled scratch.

# -- Development caches and compiler output ------------------------------------
# Empty category overrides derive beneath CADRUMO_STORAGE_ROOT. Relative paths
# anchor beneath that root; absolute paths relocate a category independently.
# Shared root of the development caches below.
CADRUMO_DEV_CACHE_ROOT=
# Development tool artifacts (reports, candidate evidence).
CADRUMO_DEV_ARTIFACTS_DIR=
# Downloaded actionlint binary.
CADRUMO_ACTIONLINT_DIR=
# Registry loader disk cache.
CADRUMO_REGISTRY_DISK_CACHE_DIR=
# Highest number of registry loader pickles kept (default 8).
# CADRUMO_REGISTRY_DISK_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES=8
# Extracted record designs.
CADRUMO_RECORD_DESIGN_CACHE_DIR=
# Extracted corpus text.
CADRUMO_CORPUS_TEXT_CACHE_DIR=
# Registry validation verdicts.
CADRUMO_REGISTRY_VERDICT_CACHE_DIR=
# Downloaded runtime wheels.
CADRUMO_RUNTIME_WHEEL_CACHE_DIR=
# Byte ceiling of the runtime wheel cache (default 8589934592).
# CADRUMO_RUNTIME_WHEEL_CACHE_BYTES=8589934592
# Native build output root.
CADRUMO_NATIVE_BUILD_ROOT=
# Documentation build output root.
CADRUMO_DOCS_BUILD_ROOT=
# Native build log verbosity: ERROR|WARNING|NOTICE|STATUS|VERBOSE|DEBUG|TRACE (default STATUS).
# CADRUMO_BUILD_LOG_LEVEL=STATUS
# Homebrew and Scoop package-channel roots.
CADRUMO_HOMEBREW_ROOT=
CADRUMO_SCOOP_ROOT=
# Package-channel installation targets default beneath storage. When exercising
# an existing package manager, explicitly select its actual prefix here; scripts
# refuse a mismatched installed prefix rather than silently using a host default.
CADRUMO_HOMEBREW_PREFIX=
CADRUMO_SCOOP_INSTALL_ROOT=
# Package-manager cache, log and scratch directories.
CADRUMO_HOMEBREW_CACHE_DIR=
CADRUMO_HOMEBREW_LOGS_DIR=
# Homebrew requires its temporary directory on the same filesystem as its prefix.
CADRUMO_HOMEBREW_TEMP_DIR=
CADRUMO_SCOOP_CACHE_DIR=
# Cache and state directories of external tools, relocated beneath storage.
CADRUMO_PYTHON_CACHE_DIR=
CADRUMO_TOOL_CACHE_DIR=
CADRUMO_TOOL_CONFIG_DIR=
CADRUMO_TOOL_DATA_DIR=
CADRUMO_TOOL_STATE_DIR=
CADRUMO_RUFF_CACHE_DIR=
CADRUMO_CARGO_HOME=
CADRUMO_CARGO_TARGET_DIR=
CADRUMO_NPM_CACHE_DIR=
CADRUMO_PIP_CACHE_DIR=
# Local model runtime locations and the GNOME extensions directory.
CADRUMO_OLLAMA_MODELS_DIR=
CADRUMO_OLLAMA_HOME_DIR=
CADRUMO_GNOME_EXTENSIONS_DIR=

# -- Documentation delivery (Cloudflare R2 + Worker) ---------------------------
# Read only by the documentation publisher and Wrangler, never by the product.
# CI holds the same names as secrets in the `docs` environment. Every
# credential here is dedicated to Cadrumo's documentation: never reuse a token
# or R2 key issued to another site.
#
# Cloudflare account that owns the documentation bucket and Worker.
# Obtain: dashboard > Workers & Pages > Account details > Account ID.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# API token that deploys the documentation Worker and its routes.
# Obtain: Manage Account > Account API Tokens > Create Token > Custom token:
#   Account  Workers Scripts        Edit
#   Account  Workers R2 Storage     Edit
#   Account  Account Settings       Read
#   Zone     Workers Routes         Edit   (zone resource: neve.md only)
#   Zone     Zone                   Read   (zone resource: neve.md only)
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# Private R2 bucket holding one releases/<tag>/ prefix per published release.
# Obtain: R2 Object Storage > Create bucket, public access off.
CADRUMO_DOCS_R2_BUCKET=
# R2 S3-compatible key that uploads release files to that bucket only.
# Obtain: R2 Object Storage > Manage API tokens > Create Account API token:
#   Object Read & Write, applied to the documentation bucket only.
CADRUMO_DOCS_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# Secret for the R2 key above; shown once, at creation.
CADRUMO_DOCS_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# -- Third-party model plugins -------------------------------------------------
# Not a Cadrumo setting, and deliberately left unassigned here: the `aeat`,
# TUI and MCP hosts set PYDANTIC_DISABLE_PLUGINS=__all__ themselves before
# their first model build. Pydantic otherwise scans every installed
# distribution's entry points on that build (about a tenth of a second per
# process), and a third-party plugin would observe taxpayer models. Export
# PYDANTIC_DISABLE_PLUGINS with your own value to opt back in; the hosts
# leave an explicitly set value alone.
